WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.534 --> 00:00:14.314
head spun.

2
00:00:14.995 --> 00:00:18.136
Morb was going to steal all of Magica's magic energy!

3
00:00:19.017 --> 00:00:19.717
Morb chuckled.

4
00:00:19.938 --> 00:00:22.779
"I can understand why you're all upset."

5
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.840
He turned to face Darb.

6
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:27.422
"Except for you, perhaps.

7
00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:30.524
Voids like you can rule Magica now.

8
00:00:31.092 --> 00:00:34.035
You'll never have to put up with being mistreated again."

9
00:00:34.915 --> 00:00:38.399
He scowled for a moment, his eyes angry and faraway.

10
00:00:38.999 --> 00:00:40.500
Then he glanced at Wyssa.

11
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.545
"By the way, you can mark this off as another world that you've destroyed."

12
00:00:45.565 --> 00:00:47.526
"Huh?" Zann said.

13
00:00:47.546 --> 00:00:50.029
"You can't blame her for what you're doing."

14
00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:52.170
"Oh, but I can."

15
00:00:52.671 --> 00:00:53.412
Morb smirked.

16
00:00:53.432 --> 00:00:58.076
"She taught me everything she knew about magical contraptions."

17
00:00:59.216 --> 00:01:01.537
Zann traded a confused look with his friends.

18
00:01:02.317 --> 00:01:03.777
What was Morb talking about?

19
00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:10.559
"I thought magical contraptions were invented right here in Magica, during the Old Times," Perda said.

20
00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:14.820
"Don't they teach you kids any real Magica history?"

21
00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:16.521
Morb rolled his eyes.

22
00:01:17.521 --> 00:01:18.741
Zann turned to Wyssa.

23
00:01:19.362 --> 00:01:20.882
"What is he talking about?"

24
00:01:21.642 --> 00:01:22.522
Wyssa looked pale.

25
00:01:22.542 --> 00:01:24.083
"It's true.

26
00:01:24.823 --> 00:01:28.164
During the Old Times, the vortex was much smaller.

27
00:01:28.872 --> 00:01:32.515
Many worlds had yet to develop, or to connect to the others."

28
00:01:33.816 --> 00:01:35.437
"Yes," Morb said.

29
00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:39.200
"That made the vortex much easier to navigate."

30
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:41.963
"Indeed." Wyssa nodded.

31
00:01:41.983 --> 00:01:46.907
"Back then people from different worlds shared their ideas and techniques.

32
00:01:47.427 --> 00:01:50.910
Many of the relics from the Cave of the Unknown came from other worlds."

33
00:01:52.151 --> 00:01:54.192
"Like the Horn of the Otherworld," Darb said.

34
00:01:54.212 --> 00:01:56.975
"It came from a beast from another world, right?"

35
00:01:56.995 --> 00:01:59.484
"Yes," Wyssa said.

36
00:01:59.504 --> 00:02:06.249
"And many forms of magic originated in other worlds, including the contraptions that Morb has built."

37
00:02:06.269 --> 00:02:13.173
"But the idiots who took over during the Days of Discipline banned those types of magic," Morb said.

38
00:02:13.193 --> 00:02:16.936
"They didn't want magic to be available to everyone.

39
00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.057
They wanted to control it."

40
00:02:19.898 --> 00:02:23.340
"That's not why they banned those types of magic," Wyssa said.

41
00:02:24.096 --> 00:02:29.498
"It was because old King Zanta, the last king of the Old Times, was an evil tyrant.

42
00:02:30.098 --> 00:02:32.838
He used magical contraptions to control people.

43
00:02:33.299 --> 00:02:35.719
He caused all sorts of chaos in Magica."

44
00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.060
"I've read about that," Darb said.

45
00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.961
"The people rose up against King Zanta.

46
00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:43.241
That's how the Days of Discipline began."

47
00:02:43.261 --> 00:02:45.302
"There's something else."

48
00:02:45.822 --> 00:02:47.162
Wyssa focused on Zann.

49
00:02:48.023 --> 00:02:52.164
"You are a direct descendant of King Zanta himself."

50
00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:54.137
Zann gasped.

51
00:02:54.837 --> 00:02:57.358
"Really?" His friends looked stunned.

52
00:02:58.179 --> 00:02:59.720
Even Morb seemed surprised.

53
00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.122
"Are you inventing lies to distract me, old woman?"

54
00:03:04.462 --> 00:03:05.042
he demanded.

55
00:03:05.843 --> 00:03:06.483
"Not at all.

56
00:03:07.084 --> 00:03:10.125
That's why their names are similar," Wyssa said.

57
00:03:11.446 --> 00:03:12.987
Zann shook his head slowly.

58
00:03:13.007 --> 00:03:15.748
"Mom said my name was an old family name."

59
00:03:16.609 --> 00:03:17.129
He gulped.

60
00:03:17.149 --> 00:03:19.770
"I never asked where it came from though."

61
00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:23.684
"She probably doesn't know its full history," Wyssa said.

62
00:03:23.704 --> 00:03:27.385
"Most of that era has been long forgotten."

63
00:03:28.426 --> 00:03:30.406
"Enough of this talk," Morb spat out.

64
00:03:31.406 --> 00:03:35.228
He touched his fingers together and sent a sizzling blast of energy toward Wyssa.

65
00:03:36.608 --> 00:03:38.689
Gliss screamed and the others gasped.

66
00:03:39.929 --> 00:03:43.810
But Wyssa raised her hand and the blast bounced away, hitting a troll.

67
00:03:44.530 --> 00:03:47.871
As the troll raced off, wailing in pain, Wyssa smirked.

68
00:03:48.611 --> 00:03:50.632
"Nice try, Morb," she said.

69
00:03:51.456 --> 00:03:57.360
"You'll have to work harder than that to Her voice trailed off as the sudden clicking of antennae

70
00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.141
filled the air.

71
00:03:59.221 --> 00:04:00.222
Zann spun around.

72
00:04:01.063 --> 00:04:04.745
The hut was swarming with the same beetles he'd seen in the Far Frontier.

73
00:04:04.765 --> 00:04:07.867
"No," Wyssa whispered, backing away.

74
00:04:08.788 --> 00:04:10.929
She tripped over a rough spot of ground and fell.

75
00:04:10.949 --> 00:04:15.612
"Wyssa!" Perda cried as the beetles swarmed over the old woman.

76
00:04:15.632 --> 00:04:17.294
"Get them off!"

77
00:04:17.734 --> 00:04:18.314
Zann yelled.

78
00:04:19.115 --> 00:04:20.416
He grabbed at one of the insects.

79
00:04:20.972 --> 00:04:23.234
But the beetle slipped away before he could get a grip.

80
00:04:24.234 --> 00:04:25.515
"Use a Blast spell!"

81
00:04:25.875 --> 00:04:28.057
Perda rubbed her hands together to create friction.

82
00:04:28.697 --> 00:04:30.639
But suddenly her movements slowed.

83
00:04:31.579 --> 00:04:33.100
Zann tried to rush over to Perda.

84
00:04:33.381 --> 00:04:35.462
But his body was moving in slow motion too!

85
00:04:35.482 --> 00:04:37.443
"It's a spell."

86
00:04:38.104 --> 00:04:40.745
Gliss lifted a hand slowly and pointed at Morb.

87
00:04:42.106 --> 00:04:44.148
Morb threw back his head and laughed.

88
00:04:45.048 --> 00:04:48.991
"Oh, why didn't I think to use a Sloth spell on you kids before?

89
00:04:49.351 --> 00:04:51.133
That would have saved me a lot of trouble!"

90
00:04:52.173 --> 00:04:54.055
Zann slowly turned to look at Wyssa.

91
00:04:54.875 --> 00:04:56.697
She was completely covered in bugs.

92
00:04:57.717 --> 00:04:59.098
"What are those things, anyway?"

93
00:04:59.379 --> 00:05:00.019
Darb asked.

94
00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:01.900
Morb smiled.

95
00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:05.703
"Ah, it's nice to see a Void with some curiosity.

96
00:05:06.424 --> 00:05:12.208
Blank bugs are loosely related to dragons, though they have none of a dragon's cunning or individuality.

97
00:05:12.716 --> 00:05:17.239
They're mindless drones with little intelligence and even less free will.

98
00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:22.802
They only follow their basic instincts: move, eat, sleep."

99
00:05:23.462 --> 00:05:24.523
His smile widened.

100
00:05:24.543 --> 00:05:31.247
"And thanks to Wyssa, every person on her home world now lives as a blank bug."

101
00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.608
"What?" Perda said.

102
00:05:34.689 --> 00:05:35.509
Morb grinned.

103
00:05:35.529 --> 00:05:38.271
"I lived there for a time, remember?

104
00:05:38.791 --> 00:05:40.332
At first they welcomed me.

105
00:05:40.864 --> 00:05:44.267
But as I gained knowledge and power, they turned against me.

106
00:05:44.908 --> 00:05:47.910
So I tricked Wyssa into helping me build a contraption.

107
00:05:48.651 --> 00:05:51.374
She had no idea what my plan was.

108
00:05:51.894 --> 00:05:55.557
But I was able to use that contraption to alter the entire population.

109
00:05:56.198 --> 00:05:58.420
Now they are all blank bugs!"

110
00:05:59.681 --> 00:06:00.962
Gliss looked horrified.

111
00:06:00.982 --> 00:06:05.726
"Now we know why Wyssa freaked out when she saw those things earlier."

112
00:06:06.707 --> 00:06:12.221
Zann shivered, imagining what it would be like to live as a mindless blank bug, or to know

113
00:06:12.261 --> 00:06:14.282
that people he cared about had to live that way.

114
00:06:14.302 --> 00:06:18.563
"Maybe that's why she's so cranky all the time," Darb murmured.

115
00:06:20.784 --> 00:06:21.824
Morb waved a hand.

116
00:06:21.844 --> 00:06:23.124
"Enough chitchat.

117
00:06:23.184 --> 00:06:24.004
I have work to do."

118
00:06:24.905 --> 00:06:29.146
He strode out of the hut, throwing up a glowing green wall to block the entrance.

119
00:06:29.966 --> 00:06:33.247
As soon as he disappeared, Zann felt the Sloth spell lift.

120
00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:36.388
"Whew!" Perda shook out her arms.

121
00:06:37.212 --> 00:06:38.673
"That spell felt weird.

122
00:06:39.274 --> 00:06:40.575
Now what are we going to do?"

123
00:06:41.216 --> 00:06:43.438
She glanced at the beetles crawling over Wyssa.

124
00:06:44.159 --> 00:06:45.660
The old woman wasn't moving.

125
00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.022
"I don't know," Zann said.

126
00:06:48.043 --> 00:06:53.007
"But we have to stop him, or Magica will lose all of its magic!"
